# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""System design scenarios (12 fields each) and FDE customer scenarios."""

# Fields: id, title, src, problem, requirements, clarify, arch (list of layer -> what), flow, tech (list (choice, why)),
#         tradeoffs, scale, failures, security, ai, followups (list (q, a)), say (2-minute answer)
DESIGNS = [
dict(id='sd-lakehouse', title='Design an enterprise lakehouse for SAP and non-SAP data', src='INFER',
 problem='A manufacturer runs S/4HANA for finance and supply chain, Salesforce for sales, and a plant IoT platform. Leadership wants one trusted view of orders-to-cash and AI assistants on top of it.',
 requirements=['Ingest SAP, CRM, IoT and file data, batch and near-real-time', 'Trusted gold data products for finance and supply chain', 'Governed access, PII protection, audit', 'Serve BI, data science and AI agents from one copy', 'Reconcile with SAP reports'],
 clarify=['Which SAP systems and which extraction paths are licensed and supported in this landscape? (VERIFY with SAP documentation)', 'What freshness does each use case need — daily close or minutes?', 'Data volumes and growth; number of source systems', 'Residency and regulatory constraints (EU data, PII)', 'Who are the consumers, and what tools do they already use?', 'Existing platforms to integrate with rather than replace'],
 arch=[('Sources', 'S/4HANA (via SAP-supported extraction), Salesforce API, IoT via Kafka, files via SFTP/object storage'), ('Ingestion', 'Kafka + CDC for change streams; batch extract jobs for bulk; all land unchanged'), ('Bronze', 'Raw Delta tables + ingestion metadata, restricted access, PII tagged'), ('Silver', 'Typed, deduplicated, conformed keys (customer, material, plant), PII tokenised'), ('Gold', 'Star schemas and data products: order-to-cash, inventory, revenue; reconciled with SAP'), ('Governance', 'Catalogue (e.g., Unity Catalog), lineage, row/column policies, audit'), ('Orchestration', 'Airflow or Databricks Workflows; data-quality gates between layers'), ('Serving', 'SQL warehouse for BI, feature tables for ML, governed tools + vector index for agents')],
 flow='Sources → ingestion (Kafka/CDC + batch) → bronze → quality gate → silver → quality gate → gold data products → BI / ML / AI agents, with catalogue, lineage and access policies across every layer.',
 tech=[('Delta Lake', 'ACID, MERGE for CDC, time travel for recovery, open format'), ('Spark / Databricks', 'Scale-out transforms, streaming and batch on one engine'), ('Kafka', 'Durable, replayable ingestion of change streams and IoT'), ('Airflow', 'Cross-system orchestration, if the customer already runs it'), ('Catalogue with fine-grained policies', 'One place to enforce access for humans and agents')],
 tradeoffs=['ELT with raw retention (replay, audit) vs ETL at the edge (less sensitive data stored) — hybrid: tokenise PII at ingestion', 'Streaming for IoT and order status vs batch for finance close', 'Copy SAP data into the lakehouse vs federate/virtualise — copying gives performance and joins with non-SAP data; federation keeps semantics and avoids copies (VERIFY SAP options such as Business Data Cloud / zero-copy sharing)', 'One platform vs keep the existing warehouse for statutory reporting'],
 scale=['Partition by date, cluster on business keys', 'Compaction and file-size management', 'Incremental processing (CDC + MERGE) instead of full reloads', 'Separate compute for ingestion, transformation and BI', 'Cost tags per domain'],
 failures=['Late or missing SAP extract → sensor timeout, freshness alert, gold stays on last good version marked stale', 'Schema change upstream → enforcement fails ingestion, quarantine, contract owner alerted', 'Bad transform → RESTORE Delta version, fix, backfill idempotently', 'Kafka consumer lag → autoscale, alert on freshness SLO'],
 security=['PII classified and tokenised at ingestion', 'Least-privilege groups; row filters per region/business unit; column masks', 'Customer-managed keys; private networking', 'Audit of every query, including agent queries'],
 ai=['Gold data products described in the catalogue so agents can find and use them', 'Agents query through governed tools with the user\'s identity', 'Vector index over documents built by an incremental pipeline, with ACL metadata'],
 followups=[('How do you make finance trust the numbers?', 'Reconcile gold totals with SAP reports daily, publish the reconciliation result alongside the data, and block promotion on mismatch beyond tolerance.'), ('How would you onboard a new source in a week?', 'A reusable ingestion template: config-driven landing to bronze, standard metadata, default quality checks, catalogue registration — only silver logic is custom.'), ('What would you not build in phase 1?', 'Real-time for everything, a custom catalogue, multi-agent systems. Start with one high-value data product end to end.')],
 say='I would start by clarifying which SAP systems are in scope and which extraction mechanisms are supported and licensed, the freshness each use case actually needs, and the regulatory constraints. The architecture is a medallion lakehouse on Delta. Change streams and IoT come through Kafka; bulk SAP and CRM extracts land through batch jobs; everything lands raw in bronze with PII tagged and tokenised. Silver conforms keys across SAP and non-SAP — customer, material, plant — and gold publishes data products like order-to-cash that are reconciled daily against SAP\'s own reports, because trust is the product. Quality gates block promotion between layers. A single catalogue governs access with row and column policies for analysts and agents alike, and captures lineage. Orchestration is Airflow or Databricks Workflows with idempotent, partitioned writes so retries and backfills are safe. For AI, agents use the same gold products through governed tools under the user\'s identity. Phase one is one data product end to end, then the pattern is reused.'),

dict(id='sd-rt-orders', title='Design a real-time order analytics pipeline', src='INFER',
 problem='Operations wants order volumes, delays and exceptions per region within two minutes, and an alert when orders stall.',
 requirements=['Ingest order events and status changes continuously', 'Dashboards updated within 2 minutes', 'Stalled-order alerts', 'Exactly-once counts', 'Daily reconciliation with the system of record'],
 clarify=['Event volume and peak rate', 'Is 2 minutes end-to-end freshness or dashboard refresh?', 'Are events emitted by the application, or must we capture DB changes (CDC)?', 'Definition of "stalled"', 'How late can events arrive?'],
 arch=[('Capture', 'Application events or CDC → Kafka, keyed by order_id'), ('Stream processing', 'Spark Structured Streaming: parse, dedup by event id, event-time windows with watermark'), ('Storage', 'Bronze events Delta; silver current order state (MERGE); gold windowed aggregates'), ('Alerting', 'Stream job emits stalled orders to an alert topic'), ('Serving', 'SQL warehouse / dashboard on gold; nightly batch reconcile')],
 flow='Orders DB/app → Kafka (key: order_id) → Structured Streaming (dedup, windows, state MERGE) → Delta bronze/silver/gold → dashboard; stalled orders → alert topic; nightly batch reconciles with source.',
 tech=[('Kafka', 'Ordering per order, buffering, replay'), ('Structured Streaming', 'Event-time windows, watermarks, checkpointed exactly-once to Delta'), ('Delta', 'Streaming sink and batch source in one table'), ('Dashboard on SQL warehouse', 'No separate serving store needed at this freshness')],
 tradeoffs=['Micro-batch (30 s) vs continuous — micro-batch meets 2 minutes with simpler semantics', 'Watermark length: correctness vs latency', 'Separate fast-path store (e.g., a low-latency OLAP DB) only if sub-second queries are required'],
 scale=['Partition topics by order_id; scale consumers to partitions', 'Bound state with watermarks', 'Compact streaming output tables regularly'],
 failures=['Job crash → restart from checkpoint, no duplicates', 'Late events beyond watermark → side table, batch correction', 'Poison message → dead-letter topic with reason', 'Lag growth → alert on freshness SLO, scale'],
 security=['PII stripped from the event stream used for dashboards', 'Topic ACLs', 'Dashboard row filters by region'],
 ai=['An operations agent can query the stalled-order table and draft customer notifications for approval'],
 followups=[('How do you guarantee exactly-once counts?', 'Dedup by event id within the watermark, checkpointed offsets, Delta sink idempotent per batch.'), ('What if the source cannot emit events?', 'Log-based CDC from the database into Kafka.')],
 say='Events or CDC changes go to Kafka keyed by order id, so each order\'s changes stay ordered. A Structured Streaming job deduplicates by event id, maintains current order state with MERGE into a silver Delta table, and computes event-time windowed aggregates with a watermark sized to real lateness. It also flags orders that have not progressed within the threshold and emits them to an alert topic. Checkpoints plus Delta\'s transactional sink give exactly-once results. The dashboard reads gold tables through a SQL warehouse, which meets a two-minute freshness without a separate serving store. Late events beyond the watermark go to a side table, and a nightly batch reconciles with the system of record.'),

dict(id='sd-rag', title='Design an enterprise RAG assistant over policies and SAP data', src='INFER',
 problem='Employees ask questions mixing policy documents ("what is the approval limit?") and live data ("which of my POs are pending?"). Answers must respect permissions and cite sources.',
 requirements=['Answer from documents and structured data', 'Respect each user\'s permissions', 'Citations', 'Freshness within an hour for documents, live for data', 'Evaluation and monitoring'],
 clarify=['Document volume, formats, change rate', 'Which structured data, and through which governed interface?', 'Identity provider and permission model', 'Languages', 'Acceptable latency and cost per question'],
 arch=[('Document pipeline', 'Extract → clean → chunk by structure → metadata (source, version, ACL) → embed → vector index; incremental'), ('Structured access', 'Predefined, permission-checked tools/SQL over gold data products'), ('Router', 'Classify: document Q&A, data question, or both'), ('Retrieval', 'Hybrid vector + keyword, ACL filter, rerank'), ('Generation', 'Prompt with sources, require citations, refuse if not found'), ('Gateway + observability', 'Redaction, rate limits, traces, feedback'), ('Evaluation', 'Golden set, retrieval recall, faithfulness, regression in CI')],
 flow='User → auth → router → (retrieval with ACL filter + rerank) and/or (governed data tool with user identity) → LLM with sources → answer + citations → trace + feedback.',
 tech=[('Hybrid retrieval', 'Semantic match plus exact identifiers'), ('Vector index in the governed platform', 'Keeps ACLs and lineage with the data (e.g., Databricks Vector Search or HANA Cloud vector engine — VERIFY)'), ('Predefined data tools over text-to-SQL', 'Safer and testable for enterprise data')],
 tradeoffs=['Predefined tools (safe, limited) vs text-to-SQL (flexible, riskier)', 'Chunk size: precision vs context', 'Bigger model vs cost/latency — route by complexity'],
 scale=['Incremental indexing from Delta change feed', 'Cache embeddings and frequent answers per permission scope', 'Rate limits per user'],
 failures=['Retrieval misses → "not found" rather than guessing', 'Stale index → freshness monitor', 'Model outage → fallback model or degrade to search results'],
 security=['ACL filter at retrieval, not in the prompt', 'Identity propagated to data tools', 'Treat retrieved text as untrusted (injection)', 'No raw PII in logs'],
 ai=['This is the AI system; evaluation at retrieval, answer and business level'],
 followups=[('How do you stop the assistant leaking HR documents?', 'ACL metadata on every chunk, filtered at retrieval by the user\'s groups; tests in the golden set that assert refusal.'), ('Text-to-SQL or tools?', 'Tools for known questions; text-to-SQL only over a curated semantic layer, read-only, with the user\'s permissions and query limits.')],
 say='I separate two kinds of knowledge. Documents go through an incremental pipeline: extract, chunk along structure, attach metadata including version and access-control labels, embed, and index. Structured data is not vectorised; the assistant reaches it through predefined, permission-checked tools over governed gold data products. A router decides which path a question needs. Retrieval is hybrid — vector plus keyword for identifiers — filtered by the user\'s permissions at retrieval time and reranked; the model answers only from sources with citations, and says it cannot find an answer rather than guessing. A gateway handles redaction, limits and tracing. I evaluate retrieval recall and answer faithfulness on a golden set built with the business, and gate changes in CI.'),

dict(id='sd-agent', title='Design an AI agent for an enterprise business process', src='INFER',
 problem='A procurement team wants an agent that detects material shortages, proposes purchase requisitions, and handles routine supplier questions.',
 requirements=['Read inventory, demand, supplier data', 'Draft requisitions; never post without approval', 'Explain reasoning', 'Audit trail', 'Measurable reduction in manual effort'],
 clarify=['Which actions are allowed autonomously vs with approval?', 'Systems of record and their APIs', 'Approval workflow and roles', 'Volume of cases per day', 'How success is measured today'],
 arch=[('Data layer', 'Governed data products: inventory, open POs, demand forecast, supplier master'), ('Tools', 'Read: get_stock, get_open_pos, get_supplier. Write: draft_requisition (creates draft only)'), ('Orchestration', 'Workflow for detection (scheduled), agent loop for case handling'), ('Guardrails', 'Tool allowlist, parameter validation, spend thresholds, step limits'), ('Human in the loop', 'Buyer approves drafts in their normal tool'), ('Observability + eval', 'Trace per case; task success, approval rate, edit rate')],
 flow='Scheduled shortage detection (deterministic) → case → agent gathers data via read tools → proposes requisition → draft created → buyer approves/edits → ERP posting by the existing process → outcome logged for evaluation.',
 tech=[('Deterministic detection', 'Shortage detection is a rule/forecast, not an LLM job'), ('Agent for case handling', 'Varying context and supplier communication'), ('Draft-only write tool', 'Reversible by design')],
 tradeoffs=['Autonomy vs control — start with draft-only, earn autonomy per category with data', 'Agent vs workflow — use the agent only where steps vary'],
 scale=['Batch shortage detection; agent only on flagged cases', 'Cost budget per case'],
 failures=['Hallucinated material number → tool validation rejects', 'Supplier email with injected instructions → treated as data, no write tool reachable from it', 'Model outage → cases queue for humans'],
 security=['Agent acts with the buyer\'s permissions', 'Audit every tool call', 'No direct ERP write access'],
 ai=['Evaluation: approval rate without edits, time to requisition, false-positive shortages'],
 followups=[('When would you allow automatic posting?', 'For low-value, high-confidence categories after the approval-without-edit rate is consistently high, with limits and monitoring.'), ('How do you evaluate it before go-live?', 'Replay historical shortages; compare proposals with what buyers actually ordered; review a sample with buyers.')],
 say='I would split the deterministic part from the agentic part. Shortage detection is a scheduled job over governed inventory, demand and open-PO data products — no LLM needed. Each flagged case goes to an agent whose tools are narrow and typed: read stock, read open POs, read supplier terms, and one write tool that only creates a draft requisition. Drafts land in the buyer\'s normal approval flow, so nothing reaches the ERP without a human. Tools run with the buyer\'s permissions, parameters are validated, steps and spend are capped, and every call is traced and audited. Before go-live I replay historical shortages and compare proposals with what buyers actually ordered; in production I track approval-without-edit rate, which is also the evidence for granting more autonomy later.'),

dict(id='sd-quality', title='Design a data quality and governance platform', src='INFER',
 problem='A customer has 400 pipelines and frequent "the numbers are wrong" escalations. Design a way to detect, contain and prevent data issues, with PII controls.',
 requirements=['Declarative checks on critical tables', 'Block, quarantine or warn per check', 'Freshness and volume monitoring for all tables', 'Lineage for impact analysis', 'PII discovery and policies', 'Ownership and alert routing'],
 clarify=['Which tables are business-critical?', 'Existing tools and catalogue', 'Who owns each domain?', 'Regulatory obligations'],
 arch=[('Check definitions', 'Versioned in Git next to pipelines (expectations / dbt tests / Great Expectations)'), ('Execution', 'Run at layer boundaries inside pipelines; results written to a quality results table'), ('Monitors', 'Freshness, volume, schema drift, distribution on all tables'), ('Catalogue', 'Owners, classifications (PII), lineage'), ('Policy engine', 'Tag-based masking and row filters'), ('Alerting', 'Route by owner; incident view with lineage blast radius')],
 flow='Pipeline step → checks → pass: promote; fail critical: block + alert owner; fail non-critical: quarantine rows + warn. Monitors scan all tables. Lineage shows downstream impact.',
 tech=[('Checks as code', 'Reviewed and versioned like the pipeline'), ('Quality results as data', 'Trend and SLA reporting'), ('Catalogue tags drive policies', 'PII protection follows data downstream')],
 tradeoffs=['Blocking protects consumers but delays data — tier by criticality', 'Automated anomaly detection catches unknowns but is noisy — tune and route'],
 scale=['Sample-based checks for huge tables', 'Incremental checks on new partitions only'],
 failures=['Check itself buggy → checks have tests; manual override with audit', 'Alert fatigue → ownership, severity, dedup'],
 security=['PII scanners on new columns', 'Masking by tag', 'Audit of access to PII'],
 ai=['Quality status exposed to agents: an agent should refuse or caveat answers when a data product is stale or failing checks'],
 followups=[('How do you get 400 pipelines covered?', 'Default monitors (freshness, volume, schema) everywhere automatically; hand-written checks only on the critical 10–20% first.')],
 say='Three layers. Prevent: data contracts with source owners and schema enforcement at ingestion. Detect: default monitors on every table for freshness, volume and schema drift, plus declarative checks as code on the critical tables at each layer boundary. Contain: each check has an action — block promotion for critical financial tables, quarantine rows with reasons for others — so consumers keep seeing the last good data rather than wrong data. Results are stored as data for trends and SLAs. The catalogue holds owners, PII classifications and lineage; alerts route to owners with the downstream blast radius; and tag-based policies apply masking and row filters wherever tagged data flows. I would start with default monitors everywhere and deep checks on the top tables, because that is where escalations come from.'),
]

